{"study_accession":"PRJNA1222425","secondary_study_accession":"SRP563278","title":"Stepwise activation of primary human memory CD4+ T cells","description":"CD4+ T cells are a highly differentiated cell type that maintain enough transcriptomic plasticity to cycle between activated and memory statuses. We generated RNA-seq libraries from T-cells harvested from three independent blood donors under three separate conditions: unstimulated fresh ex vivo, IL-2 only stimulated and TCR+CD28+IL-2 stimulated, conferring increasingly stronger activation signals. . Overall design: RNA-seq profiling of primary CD4+ memory T-cells, isolated from three blood donors and purified via FACS. Cells were treated with either IL-2, IL2+TCR or untreated. Donor 1 experiments were performed in triplicate, while donors 2 and 3 were performed in duplicate.","pubmed":"40018706","geo_series":"","n_samples":21,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN46781894","study_accession":"PRJNA1222425","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"donor3, IL2+TCR, replicate 2","description":"donor3, IL2+TCR, replicate 2","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM8789245","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-02-14","attributes":[["source_name","blood"],["tissue","blood"],["cell_type","primary CD4+ memory T-cells"],["donor","donor3"],["treatment","IL2+TCR activation"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR32312834","experiment_accession":"SRX27648322","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":44485894,"base_count":13345768200,"first_public":"2025-02-14","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8789245: donor3, IL2+TCR, replicate 2 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN46781895","study_accession":"PRJNA1222425","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"donor3, IL2+TCR, replicate 1","description":"donor3, IL